<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/glossary#jury-trial">Glossary</a> · Term</p><h1 class="enc-title">Jury trial</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as trial by jury</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Jury trial is a legal procedure in which a panel of citizens decides the facts of a case. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-empire">Russian Empire</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-ii-of-russia">Alexander II</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-judicial-reform-of-1864">Judicial Reform of 1864</a> introduced trial by jury along with independent courts and adversarial procedure. It was one of the most significant legal reforms of the imperial period.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/jury-trial.jpg" alt="Jury trial" width="320" height="181" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: John Morgan · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:The_Jury_by_John_Morgan.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
